# kit

kit creates plugin repositories and owns the parts they share: the layout, the generator, the root files and CI.
It is itself a plugin repository in that layout, with every skill of kind `utility` under `.agents/kit/utility/<name>/`.

The files a plugin repository vendors have one source, under `.agents/kit/utility/new-plugin/templates/repository/`.
kit's own copies of `.agents/sync_generated.py`, `.agents/sync-generated.ps1`, `.gitattributes`, `.gitignore` and
`CLAUDE.md` must stay byte-identical to those templates; the tests enforce it. Change the template first.
`kit:check` and `kit:update` read those templates and `kit:check`'s `standard.json`, the one statement of what each
repository type requires.

`.github/workflows/plugin-ci.yml` is the CI every plugin repository calls, pinned to a kit tag. Changing the
generator, a vendored file or the workflow is a kit release: bump `KIT_VERSION`, `.agents/plugins/kit.json` and the
Codex manifest version together, then tag `v<version>` after the merge.

`.codex/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`, `.agents/INDEX.md`, both marketplace files and `plugins/*` are generated. Run
`pwsh .agents/sync-generated.ps1` after authored changes; `pwsh .agents/sync-generated.ps1 -Check` and
`python -B -m unittest discover -s .agents/tests -p "test_*.py"` must pass before delivery.
{
  "_": "Codex's rung of the lane ladder. Paired name-for-name with .agents/lanes/claude.json: the same LN means the same *relative* capability on both harnesses, so a skill declares `lane: L4` once and each harness resolves it to its own model. These two files are the only two places in the repo a model name may appear. Rungs are ordered L1 (most capable) to L7 (cheapest).",

  "host": "codex",
  "effort_key": "reasoning_effort",
  "skill_supports_effort": false,
  "$comment_skill_supports_effort": "Whether this harness accepts an effort key in SKILL.md front matter. Codex does not, so a Codex skill payload gets the rung's model alone and the rung's effort reaches it only through a lane agent.",
  "model_key": "model",

  "lanes": {
    "L1": {
      "summary": "Critical design decisions or large complex plans with interacting decisions.",
      "model": "gpt-6-astra",
      "reasoning_effort": "xhigh",
      "context_ceiling": null,
      "why": "The highest lane for a critical design decision or a big, complex plan with substantial interacting decisions. Record a concrete criticality or scale reason before selecting it. A plan label, architecture, data model, contract, or mechanism choice alone does not select it. Never implementation, review or delivery."
    },
    "L2": {
      "summary": "High-stakes judgement that is not design, where a wrong call is costly or hard to undo.",
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "reasoning_effort": "xhigh",
      "context_ceiling": null,
      "why": "top general family at the setting above `high`. Judgement with a lot riding on it that designs nothing: a diagnosis of a production failure, a security or migration review. Delivering a change never selects it; merge, push and publish are governed by the delivery gates."
    },
    "L3": {
      "summary": "Open investigation or bounded uncertain design with unresolved alternatives.",
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "reasoning_effort": "high",
      "context_ceiling": null,
      "why": "top general family at its default setting. Open investigation or bounded uncertain design with unresolved alternatives, including a diagnosis with no known answer or evidence a test cannot settle."
    },
    "L4": {
      "summary": "Specified implementation, ordinary review, and small local testable choices.",
      "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
      "reasoning_effort": "high",
      "context_ceiling": null,
      "why": "the workhorse family at high effort. Specified implementation and ordinary review, including a small local mechanism choice inside a testable fix. Features, bugfixes and review lenses whose mistakes a compiler or a test suite will catch. Delivery never selects this rung."
